.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
src/*.o
src/*.so
src/*.dll
*.Rcheck/
*.tar.gz

# Leading slashes on purpose. An unanchored rule also matches the same name nested
# anywhere, which silently dropped a whole subpackage from a commit on the Python side.
/_legacy/
/examples/data/
/examples/output/
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pt
*.safetensors

# Figures produced while checking things by eye; they belong in the vignette,
# not loose in the root.
/*.png

# Bytecode from the shim, compiled by whichever Python ran the tests. It is not ours to
# ship: a .pyc is tied to one interpreter version.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The site is built by CI and deployed to the gh-pages branch, so the built copy has no
# business in history - it is several megabytes of generated HTML that would change on
# every documentation edit. `_quarto/` is altdoc's working directory and is generated the
# same way; its `_freeze/` was measured at 220s against 223s with and without, so there is
# nothing to gain by keeping it either.
/docs/
altdoc/freeze.rds
_quarto/

# altdoc regenerates this on every render - verified by deleting it and rendering - and it
# records the machine that did: `last_built` moved from 12:36 to 15:18 between two commits
# an afternoon apart, and the copy a runner published says `pandoc: 3.8.3` where this one
# says 2.9.2.1. Generated, machine-specific, and it would dirty the tree after every build.
altdoc/pkgdown.yml
